hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-8 = cons (quoted (cons "*Identity* comes from *idem*, the same, and *same* comes from the root for " (cons "one" (cons ", which also gives *simple*, *similar*, *simultaneous* and *singular*. In mathematics a singular map collapses distinctions, sending different points to one. The root of *singular* is the root of *same*. *Universe* is *unus* + *versus*, turned into one. *Univalence* is *unus* + *valere*: one worth, one strength. *Equivalence* is *aequus* + *valere*: equal in worth. So the univalence axiom says, in its own Latin, that things of equal worth are of one worth. Identity is equivalence because sameness is equal worth. *Homotopy* is Greek *homos* + *topos*, same place. Homotopy type theory is, by name, the theory of what occupies the same place. Every word in the foundation is a word about oneness, worked out precisely." nil)))) (cons "" nil)
